  "text": "Freeze a model's code, and it still gets worse. Nothing in the repository moved. The world it learned from did: new customers, new tactics, a sensor swapped for one that reports in other units. This round is everything after training: versioning, testing, shipping, and watching a model in production. Twelve questions are worked through here, and five go quickly.\n\nQuestion one. What is em-el-ops, and how does it differ from traditional DevOps? It brings DevOps practices to machine learning: automation, monitoring, and continuous integration and delivery, or CI CD. But it adds a moving part: data. A traditional app is code plus config. An ML system is code, plus data, plus the trained model they produce, and all three must be versioned, tested and reproducible. And because a model decays while its code stays frozen, monitoring and retraining are part of the job from day one.",
